Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||02-18-2001||05:42 PM||||just curious, why wouldn't you want to water cool it?<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 02-18-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000009||squid||02-18-2001||08:51 PM||||I'm sure you would shorten the life of the bushings and increased chance of cartridge cracking without water cooling. A turbo designed without water cooling would most likely have different clearances and shielding from the turbine side. It would be worth the added trouble to keep them. ||||reg||1
